# Shell scripts must be LF everywhere. These are checked out on Windows (where
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise give them CRLF) and run on the Kali host,
# where a CR at the end of the shebang fails with:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# Scoped to *.sh on purpose: the Python sources are CRLF in the working tree and
# a blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise the whole repository in one commit.
*.sh text eol=lf
